Reuse connected transport for pod commands

Add rumpel exec with direct argv execution, the pod's resolved
environment and user, and a working directory relative to the
repository. Keep enter's behavior intact.

Share the daemon's existing HTTP/2 pod event connection so connected
execs send one remote request without a readiness probe or another
handshake. Stream binary stdin, stdout, stderr, and exit status with
bounded buffers. Forward signals without DATA bodies so blocked input
cannot prevent interruption. Disable request retries and redirects
because losing a response cannot establish whether a command executed.

Use the existing pod state snapshot for merge's dirty-checkout warning,
removing the only caller of the buffered /run endpoint and eliminating
that second command execution implementation.

Keep receive capacity available across concurrent HTTP/2 streams so
stalled command input or output cannot starve unrelated executions.
